==Defense Policy==

===The Satori System===
A unique aspect of Sanese defense is the Satori System, an integrated AI-driven command network that links all SIF assets with the nation's civilian digital infrastructure. The system allows for real-time synchronization of naval fire, air defense, and army logistics. It functions as an automated deterrent, capable of activating the Deep Sky Umbrella without direct human intervention in the event of a saturation strike. The Satori network also incorporates advanced predictive algorithms, analyzing global supply chain fluctuations and maritime traffic to preemptively position SIN escorts along vulnerable sectors of the Silicon Lanes.

===Unarmed Combat (Okaiken Kakutōjutsu)===
The SIF utilizes a specialized self-defense system known as Okaiken Kakutōjutsu ({{nihongo2|岡井県格闘術}}). Adopted in 2008 and refined in 2012, the system emphasizes close-quarters knife defense, grappling, and joint manipulation. It was designed specifically for use in the cramped corridors of naval vessels and dense urban environments where traditional firearms may be impractical or highly dangerous to collateral infrastructure. All personnel, regardless of branch, must undergo basic certification in the system during their National Service, with advanced instructor courses mandatory for the Imperial Guard and Red Regiment.

===Foreign Deployments and Peacekeeping===
While the Kurosawa Doctrine limits broad international entanglements, the SIF frequently participates in targeted overseas deployments. These missions are strictly defined by their strategic value to Okaiken. The SIF has established a permanent logistical hub in the southern Cilician Ocean to support anti-piracy operations and secure lithium transport routes. Additionally, engineering battalions from the SIA are regularly dispatched to allied nations following natural disasters, leveraging their extensive domestic experience in earthquake and typhoon recovery to build diplomatic goodwill and test deployment logistics.

